<section id="private-inference" class="mt-8 border-t border-slate-200 pt-6">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">What makes inference private?</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-700 max-w-4xl">A trusted execution environment (TEE) can protect memory from the machine's host. A private inference client also needs to establish which code receives plaintext, what that code can do, and whether the actual prompt and reply use the verified keys. A genuine enclave can still run operator-controlled code that logs prompts.</p>
  <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 md:grid-cols-3 text-sm">
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4"><h3 class="font-semibold">1. Authenticate the environment</h3><p class="mt-1 text-slate-600">Check hardware evidence, its trust roots and security state. Bind it to the connection's keys and establish freshness.</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4"><h3 class="font-semibold">2. Identify the plaintext-handling code</h3><p class="mt-1 text-slate-600">Compare authenticated measurements with expected software and configuration. Include the serving application, model where claimed, and every necessary worker hop.</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4"><h3 class="font-semibold">3. Establish who can change it</h3><p class="mt-1 text-slate-600">Inspect operator access, unmeasured inputs and client update policy. A provider publishing a new hash does not mean your policy accepts it.</p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700">The table separates these obligations. <strong>A missing check in our adapter describes our method.</strong> A documented protection gap describes the reviewed system. Open a cell for the evidence, the exact missing obligation and its scope; method work is linked to issues with completion criteria. Collection describes returned attestation evidence, not inference uptime or privacy.</p>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">The <a href="./history.html" class="underline text-indigo-700">Reference values explorer</a> follows identities and policies over time. Audits explain what those values cover. Neither a stable hash nor a fresh observation renews an audit.</p>
</section>

<section id="audit-lessons" class="mt-8 border-t border-slate-200 pt-6">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">What the companion audits establish</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-700 max-w-4xl">The <a class="underline text-indigo-700" href="https://github.com/amiller/devproof-audits-guide">DevProof case studies</a> ask whether a user can verify the limits on a service operator's access and ability to change software. Beat connects that analysis to route assessments and retained reference history. These selected lessons explain the evidence behind the caution, including strengths that a generic label would hide.</p>
  <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-slate-500">{{ audit_synthesis.scope }} Curated {{ audit_synthesis.curated_at }}.</p>
  {% for study in audit_synthesis.studies %}
  <article id="audit-{{ study.id }}" class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold">{{ study.title }}</h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-700">{{ study.summary }}</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-slate-500">Evidence {{ study.evidence_date }} · <a class="underline text-indigo-700" href="{{ study.source_url }}">Pinned report and evidence ↗</a>{% for route in study.route_ids %} · <a class="underline text-indigo-700" href="./assessments.html#route-{{ route }}">{{ route }}</a>{% endfor %}</p>
    <details class="mt-3 text-sm"><summary class="cursor-pointer text-indigo-700">Finding and limits</summary>
      <p class="mt-2"><strong>Reviewed scope:</strong> {{ study.scope }}</p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">{% for finding in study.findings %}<li>{{ finding }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
      <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600"><strong>Limits:</strong> {{ study.limits }}</p>
      {% if study.additional_sources %}<p class="mt-2">{% for source in study.additional_sources %}<a class="underline text-indigo-700 mr-3" href="{{ source.url }}">{{ source.label }} ↗</a>{% endfor %}</p>{% endif %}
    </details>
  </article>
  {% endfor %}
</section>
